data.content:
All files updated. Here's a summary of the **5 breaking changes** and their fixes:

---

### Fixes Applied to This Project

| # | Breaking Change | Fix |
|---|----------------|-----|
| 1 | `HasData(DateTime.UtcNow)` → "pending model changes" exception | Replaced with fixed constant `new DateTime(2024,1,1,…)` |
| 2 | `Migrate()` inside explicit transaction now throws | Removed wrapping `ExecutionStrategy`/`BeginTransaction` — EF Core 9 manages this internally |
| 3 | `Design` package not found with SDK 9.0.200+ | Added `<Publish>true</Publish>` with explicit `<IncludeAssets>` |

### Required Fixes for the Cosmos DB Project

For your separate Cosmos DB project with existing documents, apply these in its `OnModelCreating`:

```csharp
// Breaking change 4: Discriminator renamed from "Discriminator" to "$type"
// Preserve old property name for existing documents
modelBuilder.Entity<YourEntity>().HasDiscriminator<string>("Discriminator");

// Breaking change 5: id no longer contains discriminator prefix
// Existing docs have "EntityType|Key" format — preserve that
modelBuilder.Entity<YourEntity>().HasRootDiscriminatorInJsonId(true);
```

And for **sync I/O removal** (Breaking change 6): replace all synchronous calls:

```csharp
// BREAKS in EF Core 9 Cosmos provider:
var items = db.Products.ToList();
db.SaveChanges();

// Fix — use async:
var items = await db.Products.ToListAsync();
await db.SaveChangesAsync();
```
